diwall (1.19.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * mode_conseille now filtered to successful diagnostic_dom.json runs only
    (lib/journal.py) — a mid-run failure no longer feeds a recommendation.
  * chainage traceability for declencher_scenario: rpa.py builds an ordered
    call tree, lib/journal.py records it, journal.py renders it as an
    indented tree per matching entry — absent on runs without chaining.
  * Guide-read lock re-armed: notice-version 3.6 -> 3.7 (lib/preflight_guide.py
    resynchronised in the same commit).
  * scripts/verifier-coherence.sh (git source only, not packaged): static
    doc/code coherence check (notice-version vs index table, argparse flags
    vs docs).
  * Documentation: --ignorer-waf decision rule, etat's declarative nature
    clarified (not a gate), guide-lock's cooperative-nature limit documented,
    iframe_chemin depth guidance, reference-safe assertion guidance for
    --replay-verifier, zero-delay guidance for local targets, new
    docs/ACCESS_OBSERVATIONS.md registry.
  * postinst: create /opt/diwall/references/ (770 root:diwall) — missing
    from the initial packaging, caught by a real install/remove test on
    this very cycle (watch.py --sauver-reference failed with
    PermissionError on a fresh install). install.sh already created this
    directory; postinst did not.
  * postinst: chmod 755 on shot.py/watch.py/rpa.py/journal.py — missing
    from the initial packaging (dh_fixperms leaves regular files at 644).
    watch.py invokes shot.py as a direct subprocess relying on the shebang
    and execute bit, not "python3 shot.py" — failed with PermissionError
    on a fresh install. The git-clone channel's deploy.sh already sets this.

